  "learn": {
    "title": "Two Clocks",
    "body": "Wire red D9 → 220 Ω → LED → GND and green D10 → 220 Ω → LED → GND. Each LED needs its own resistor. Wire the button between D2 and GND with INPUT_PULLUP.\n\nToggle red every 200 ms (400 ms full period) and green every 350 ms (700 ms full period). Give each task its own unsigned long timestamp. Also count falling edges on D2 and print PRESS=1, PRESS=2.\n\nRun for at least three seconds and press twice, releasing between presses. Both rhythms must continue while the input is read. A chain of delay() calls couples the clocks and misses input; schedule each task with millis() instead. This exercise assumes clean button presses; reuse the previous debounce pattern for physical switches.",
    "links": []
  },
